---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hanfu Guide: Best Cities, Costs & Tips | ChinaStyle"
  description="Complete Hanfu travel guide: Xi'an, Luoyang, Chengdu rental shops, costs, best seasons for photoshoots, where to stay near city walls, and full trip tips."
  ogImage="/images/og-hanfu.webp"
  canonicalUrl="/hanfu"
  articleDate="2026-08-03"
  breadcrumbs={{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Experiences", url: "/hanfu/" }}>
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#b5343a] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase">Hanfu Experience Guide</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">
        Hanfu: Where to Wear China''s Most Ancient Attire
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Hanfu (漢服) — the flowing robes of the Han Chinese — has exploded back into the mainstream. The best way to experience it isn''t through a screen. It''s standing on Xi''an''s 600-year-old city wall at sunset, sleeves catching the breeze.
      </p>

      <!-- Quick jump -->
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="#cities" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 bg-stone-100 rounded-full text-stone-600 hover:bg-stone-200 transition-colors">Best Cities</a>
        <a href="#getting-there" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 bg-stone-100 rounded-full text-stone-600 hover:bg-stone-200 transition-colors">How to Get There</a>
        <a href="#stay" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 bg-stone-100 rounded-full text-stone-600 hover:bg-stone-200 transition-colors">Where to Stay</a>
        <a href="#cost" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 bg-stone-100 rounded-full text-stone-600 hover:bg-stone-200 transition-colors">Cost Breakdown</a>
        <a href="#experience" class="text-xs px-3 py-1.5 bg-stone-100 rounded-full text-stone-600 hover:bg-stone-200 transition-colors">Step-by-Step</a>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== BEST CITIES ===== -->
      <h2 id="cities" class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-16 mb-4">Best Cities for Hanfu Experiences</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a]/10 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
            <span class="text-[#b5343a] font-bold text-sm">1</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Xi''an <span class="text-xs font-normal text-[#b5343a] ml-2">Top Choice</span></h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Over 500 Hanfu rental shops near the city wall and Daming Palace. Rent a full set (clothing + hair + makeup) for 150-400 RMB. Shoot on the ancient city wall (entry 54 RMB), at Daming Palace ruins, or in Datang Everbright City at night. The wall at sunset is the most iconic shot — golden light on ancient brick with Tang dynasty robes.</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-stone-400 mt-2"><strong>Best spot:</strong> South Gate (Yongningmen) has the highest concentration of shops and photogenic backdrops.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a]/10 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
            <span class="text-[#b5343a] font-bold text-sm">2</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Luoyang</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Luoyang Old Town and the area around Longmen Grottoes have a thriving Hanfu scene. The peony-themed Tang dynasty styles are unique to this city. Rentals are cheaper than Xi''an — 100-250 RMB for a full set. Photograph in front of the Longmen Grottoes carvings or in the peony gardens (best in April).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a]/10 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
            <span class="text-[#b5343a] font-bold text-sm">3</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Chengdu</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Jinli Ancient Street is a Hanfu hotspot — locals and tourists stroll in period costume. Combine Hanfu with a traditional tea ceremony in a Sichuan teahouse. Shu embroidery workshops in Chengdu let you see the craft behind the garments. 100-300 RMB for rental.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a]/10 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
            <span class="text-[#b5343a] font-bold text-sm">4</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Hangzhou</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Song dynasty hanfu by West Lake is understated elegance at its finest. The China National Silk Museum offers free costume try-on sessions. Best in spring (March-April) when the willow trees along the lake are at their greenest. 80-250 RMB for rental.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a]/10 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
            <span class="text-[#b5343a] font-bold text-sm">5</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Nanjing</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Ming dynasty hanfu at Ming Xiaoling Mausoleum — the red walls and imperial architecture are the ultimate backdrop. Nanjing also has excellent silk brocade (yunjin) workshops that explain the fabric behind the fashion. 100-300 RMB.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== GETTING THERE ===== -->
      <h2 id="getting-there" class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-16 mb-4">How to Get to Each City</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead><tr class="border-b border-stone-200 text-left"><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-stone-800">City</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-stone-800">Nearest Airport</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-stone-800">From Airport to City</th><th class="py-3 font-semibold text-stone-800">Best Train Connections</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">Xi''an</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Xi''an Xianyang (XIY)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Metro Line 14, 40 min, 8 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">4.5 hrs from Beijing, 3 hrs from Chengdu</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">Luoyang</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Luoyang Beijiao (LYA)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Airport bus, 40 min, 15 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">1.5 hrs from Xi''an by high-speed train</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">Chengdu</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Chengdu Tianfu (TFU)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Metro Line 18, 50 min, 10 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">3 hrs from Xi''an, 9 hrs from Kunming</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">Hangzhou</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Hangzhou Xiaoshan (HGH)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Metro Line 1/7, 50 min, 8 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">45 min from Shanghai, 1.5 hrs from Nanjing</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-medium">Nanjing</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Nanjing Lukou (NKG)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Metro Line S1, 40 min, 7 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">1 hr from Shanghai, 1.5 hrs from Hangzhou</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-stone-400 mt-3">All airports listed have international connections. If arriving internationally, Beijing (PEK/PKX), Shanghai (PVG), and Guangzhou (CAN) are the main gateways with the most flight options.</p>

      <!-- ===== WHERE TO STAY ===== -->
      <h2 id="stay" class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-16 mb-4">Where to Stay</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">For a Hanfu-focused trip, staying within walking distance of the key Hanfu districts saves time on costume changes and transport.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 text-sm">Xi''an: Near South Gate (Yongningmen)</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">Hotels within 10-minute walk of the city wall South Gate. The Tang Dynasty Art Garden Hotel and nearby boutique hotels put you steps from Hanfu shops. District: Beilin. Budget: 250-500 RMB/night for a good mid-range hotel.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 text-sm">Luoyang: Old Town District</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">Stay in Luoyang Old Town (老城) near Lijing Gate. Walking distance to costume rentals and the atmospheric old streets. Budget: 150-300 RMB/night.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 text-sm">Chengdu: Wuhou or Jinli Area</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">The area around Wuhou Shrine and Jinli Ancient Street has a high concentration of Hanfu shops and teahouses. Budget: 200-400 RMB/night.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 text-sm">Hangzhou: West Lake North Shore</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">Hotels along Beishan Road face West Lake directly — wake up to the view you''ll photograph in Hanfu. 10-minute taxi to the Silk Museum. Budget: 300-600 RMB/night.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== COST ===== -->
      <h2 id="cost" class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-16 mb-4">Cost Breakdown for a Hanfu Day</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead><tr class="border-b border-stone-200 text-left"><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-stone-800">Item</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-stone-800">Basic</th><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-stone-800">Standard</th><th class="py-3 font-semibold text-stone-800">Premium</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Costume rental (2-4 hrs)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">100-150 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">200-300 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">400+ RMB</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Basic hairstyling</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Included</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Included</td><td class="py-2.5">Included</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Professional makeup</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">DIY only</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">+50-100 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">+150-200 RMB</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Accessories (fan, umbrella)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">+20-40 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Included</td><td class="py-2.5">Full set included</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Professional photographer</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">N/A (selfie)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">+500-800 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">+1,000-1,500 RMB</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Attraction entry (e.g., city wall)</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">54 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">54 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5">54 RMB</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold">Total for the day</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold">170-250 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold">800-1,250 RMB</td><td class="py-2.5 font-semibold">1,600-2,350 RMB</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- ===== STEP BY STEP ===== -->
      <h2 id="experience" class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-16 mb-4">What to Expect: Step-by-Step</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold">1</div>
          <div><h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Choose Your Shop</h4><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Walk-ins welcome at most Hanfu shops. For discounts, book via Meituan (美团) or Xiaohongshu (小红书) — typically 20-30% off walk-in prices. Search "汉服体验" (Hanfu experience) + the city name. Look at recent customer photos to judge quality.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold">2</div>
          <div><h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Pick Your Dynasty & Style</h4><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Shops typically stock 50-200 sets organized by dynasty. Tang dynasty: bold colors, chest-high ruqun (most photogenic). Song dynasty: elegant restraint, narrow sleeves. Ming dynasty: regal structure, stand-collar aoqun. Tell the staff which look you want, or show a reference photo. Allow 15-20 minutes for selection and fitting.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold">3</div>
          <div><h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Hair & Makeup (20-30 min)</h4><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Stylists create dynasty-appropriate looks using traditional hairpins, flowers, and hairpieces. Tang styles are elaborate with high buns and floral ornaments. Song styles are simpler with low buns. Communicate any preferences early — once they start pinning, changes take time.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold">4</div>
          <div><h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Head Out & Shoot</h4><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Rental periods are usually 2-4 hours. Leave a deposit (200-500 RMB, refundable) and an ID. Walk to your chosen location. If you booked a photographer, they''ll guide you to the best spots and poses. If self-shooting, golden hour (1 hour before sunset) is the best light. The city wall closes at different times by season — check before heading out.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#b5343a] text-white flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold">5</div>
          <div><h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900">Return & Get Your Photos</h4><p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mt-1 leading-relaxed">Return the costume by the agreed time. Most shops send digital photos within 24-48 hours via WeChat. Ask for unedited RAW files if you want to edit yourself — some photographers charge extra for the full set.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 p-6 bg-[#b5343a]/5 border border-[#b5343a]/20 rounded-xl">
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700"><strong>Ready to plan your Hanfu trip?</strong> Check our <a href="/plan-trip" class="text-[#b5343a] underline font-medium">Plan Your Trip guide</a> for visa info, itineraries, and full budget breakdowns.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-stone-200 text-center">
        <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-lg font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-3">Sources & Further Reading</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-stone-500 inline-block text-left">
          <li>&bull; <a href="https://en.chinaculture.org/" class="text-[#b5343a] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">China Culture.org</a> — Ministry of Culture official resource on Chinese heritage and traditions</li>
          <li>&bull; <a href="https://en.dpm.org.cn/" class="text-[#b5343a] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Palace Museum</a> (Forbidden City, Beijing) — original imperial robes and textile collections</li>
          <li>&bull; <a href="https://www.chinasilkmuseum.com/" class="text-[#b5343a] hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">China National Silk Museum</a> (Hangzhou) — world''s largest silk and textile museum</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
</BaseLayout>
